menu "doom-esp32 brain link"

    config DOOM_BRAIN_PLAY
        bool "Let the STM32 brain play (start a real game instead of the attract demos)"
        default y
        help
            Starts E1M1 directly and drives the player from the brain's replies. Without the
            brain connected the player stands still. Turn off to get the attract demos back.

    config DOOM_BRAIN_MAP
        int "Episode 1 map to start on (E1M<n>)"
        range 1 9
        default 2
        depends on DOOM_BRAIN_PLAY
        help
            E1M1's start room is empty (its nearest monster is about 1700 map units away), and
            the player only reacts to what is on screen. E1M2 at skill 3 has 11 monsters
            within 1000 units of the start.

    config DOOM_BRAIN_SKILL
        int "Skill level (1 easiest .. 5 hardest)"
        range 1 5
        default 3
        depends on DOOM_BRAIN_PLAY

    config DOOM_BRAIN_LEARN
        bool "Let the brain learn while playing (reward-modulated plasticity on the STM32)"
        default y
        depends on DOOM_BRAIN_PLAY
        help
            Sends BRAIN_STEP_FLAG_LEARN with a reward: +1 per monster the player kills, minus
            health lost / 100. Only while the player is alive in a level. The STM32 keeps the
            learned weights in RAM until it is reset or power cycled. Off: the connectome
            weights (or whatever the STM32 learned before) are used unchanged.

    config DOOM_BRAIN_RESET_WEIGHTS_ON_BOOT
        bool "Return the brain to the connectome weights when the ESP32 boots"
        default n
        depends on DOOM_BRAIN_PLAY
        help
            Sends BRAIN_STEP_FLAG_RESET_WEIGHTS once, with the first STEP after boot. Off: what
            the brain learned survives an ESP32 reboot as long as the STM32 stays powered.

    config DOOM_BRAIN_TX_GPIO
        int "ESP32 TX GPIO (to STM32 PB7 / Nucleo D0)"
        default 17
        help
            GPIO17 and 18 are free on the ESP32-S3 N16R8 (not flash, PSRAM, USB, UART0, strapping
            or the OLED's GPIO8/9).

    config DOOM_BRAIN_RX_GPIO
        int "ESP32 RX GPIO (from STM32 PB6 / Nucleo D1)"
        default 18

    config DOOM_BRAIN_BAUD
        int "Link baud rate"
        default 115200

endmenu
